WEBVTT

00:45.713 --> 00:47.590
CHAPTER 32:
A VARIABLE CALLED NA DEUL-I

00:47.673 --> 00:49.842
-How have you been?
-Good.

00:51.510 --> 00:53.387
You seem to be doing well too.
I'm happy for you.

00:57.475 --> 01:00.352
To tell the truth,
I was surprised to hear from you.

01:00.436 --> 01:01.437
Pleased too.

01:02.855 --> 01:05.149
You could have gotten in touch yourself.

01:10.613 --> 01:11.697
Are you doing better now?

01:12.281 --> 01:13.449
Yeah.

01:13.532 --> 01:16.368
When I heard you had a surgery,
I was really worried.

01:16.452 --> 01:17.745
And I couldn't get hold of you.

01:20.289 --> 01:21.791
I'm sorry I didn't say anything.

01:22.458 --> 01:24.210
I was in shock.

01:25.169 --> 01:26.378
And I was really upset too.

01:28.088 --> 01:29.882
I can't believe you majored in Education
and became a teacher.

01:30.341 --> 01:31.342
It was so unexpected.

01:31.425 --> 01:33.844
I was sure you'd stick with research.

01:56.700 --> 01:57.952
Eui-ju?

01:58.619 --> 01:59.453
What are you doing here?

01:59.537 --> 02:00.871
EPISODE 10

02:01.872 --> 02:02.748
Sir.

02:02.832 --> 02:05.417
Oh, I was just doing some studying,

02:05.501 --> 02:06.919
but it's time to go home.

02:07.002 --> 02:08.295
Eui-ju.

02:08.379 --> 02:10.840
Have you finally decided
to put some effort into your studies?

02:11.549 --> 02:12.383
Yes.

02:15.886 --> 02:17.638
What brought you here, Mr. Ha?

02:18.264 --> 02:19.348
Is that Mr. Ga?

02:20.683 --> 02:22.184
What do we have here?

02:22.268 --> 02:25.104
My dear Mr. Ga, the standoffish robot,
is enjoying coffee with someone.

02:25.187 --> 02:26.313
With a lady friend, no less.

02:27.648 --> 02:28.774
Hang on a second.

02:29.483 --> 02:30.484
By any chance…

02:32.528 --> 02:34.405
You're Professor Na Deul-i, right?

02:36.699 --> 02:37.741
Yes, that's me.

02:39.285 --> 02:40.953
I knew it. I saw you on the news.

02:41.036 --> 02:44.665
I was touched by the interview you gave
after winning the Fields Medal.

02:44.748 --> 02:46.333
Oh, thank you.

02:47.459 --> 02:48.586
Where are my manners?

02:48.669 --> 02:51.297
It's nice to meet you.
I'm a colleague of Mr. Ga's.

02:51.380 --> 02:53.591
My name is Ha E-den. It's such a pleasure.

02:59.513 --> 03:03.976
Anyhow, how do you know Mr. Ga?

03:05.477 --> 03:06.312
We're friends.

03:06.395 --> 03:09.857
Friends. I see.

03:09.940 --> 03:11.942
When a man and woman
meet in a cafe on the weekend,

03:12.026 --> 03:13.944
it's a date 99% of the time, no?

03:15.988 --> 03:16.822
Shall we get going?

03:17.364 --> 03:18.198
-Yes.
-Okay.

03:18.282 --> 03:21.952
You two look great together.

03:22.036 --> 03:23.996
You make a great couple.

03:24.079 --> 03:25.122
See you again soon.

03:25.205 --> 03:26.457
-Oh, sure.
-Take care.

03:27.416 --> 03:28.834
As for you, study hard!

03:28.918 --> 03:31.003
If you want to become
as great as Professor Na.

03:31.795 --> 03:33.005
Get home safely.

03:36.759 --> 03:37.676
Hop on.

03:38.469 --> 03:39.428
Thank you.

03:40.137 --> 03:41.180
Hello.

03:42.431 --> 03:44.350
My name is Yeo Eui-ju.

03:44.433 --> 03:47.144
Mr. Ga is my homeroom teacher.

03:47.978 --> 03:50.356
I see. Hello.

03:51.065 --> 03:52.775
Wow, that's amazing.

03:52.858 --> 03:54.693
I can't believe
you have a student of your own.

03:56.028 --> 03:58.822
Were you at college with Mr. Ga?

03:58.906 --> 04:01.450
No, we've been friends
since middle school.

04:02.242 --> 04:04.078
I see. Middle school?

04:05.162 --> 04:06.163
That's a long time.

04:06.246 --> 04:07.414
You'd best get going.

04:08.290 --> 04:09.667
About that thing I suggested.

04:10.334 --> 04:11.543
You'll give it some thought?

04:12.962 --> 04:14.254
I'm not sure.

04:14.922 --> 04:16.757
Are you playing hard to get or what?

04:17.716 --> 04:18.676
Get going already.

04:18.759 --> 04:20.427
All right.

04:20.511 --> 04:22.638
Until next time, Eui-ju.

04:23.389 --> 04:25.224
Okay, goodbye.

04:25.307 --> 04:26.433
Drive safe.

04:39.279 --> 04:41.573
Mr. Ga, your friend

04:41.657 --> 04:43.200
seems really nice.

04:43.283 --> 04:46.537
She's pretty, and she seems really kind.

04:47.204 --> 04:49.665
And she even won the Fields Medal.

04:49.748 --> 04:51.250
That's so cool.

04:51.333 --> 04:52.876
I wish I had a friend like that.

04:54.253 --> 04:56.588
I bet she's super popular.

04:56.672 --> 04:58.257
She must have a boyfriend, right?

04:59.133 --> 05:02.803
Would it be difficult to find someone
when you're as perfect as her?

05:02.886 --> 05:04.888
When you're good at everything,

05:04.972 --> 05:07.933
people would always compare
your partner to you,

05:08.017 --> 05:10.394
making them feel insecure.

05:12.980 --> 05:14.023
What are you trying to say?

05:15.399 --> 05:16.859
It's just

05:16.942 --> 05:20.863
I was wondering what kind of guy
someone so amazing would date.

05:21.905 --> 05:22.740
Why?

05:25.325 --> 05:28.245
If you don't get more than 50 points
in the upcoming math exam,

05:29.079 --> 05:31.540
I'm telling your parents about your novel
at our parent-teacher meeting.

05:33.917 --> 05:34.752
Sorry?

05:35.544 --> 05:37.212
Come on, that's not fair.

05:37.296 --> 05:39.548
Sir, you won't really, will you?

05:39.631 --> 05:41.175
Please tell me you won't. Come on.

05:43.093 --> 05:44.636
Sir!

05:44.720 --> 05:48.515
I'll try my best,
but 50 points in math is a tall order.

05:50.225 --> 05:54.146
Sir, that thing your friend
was talking about just now.

05:54.897 --> 05:56.732
What did she want you to think over?

05:57.524 --> 05:59.026
It's not really any of your business.

05:59.818 --> 06:01.904
Would it kill you to be nicer?

06:03.739 --> 06:04.740
Don't forget my coke.

06:05.616 --> 06:06.825
Just a moment, sir.

06:07.451 --> 06:09.036
I'll be right back.

06:09.912 --> 06:11.455
Hold up.

06:11.538 --> 06:13.123
Don't go.

06:13.207 --> 06:14.291
Wait for me, okay?

06:23.425 --> 06:24.426
Got it.

06:27.304 --> 06:29.515
Don't forget the factors
associated with constipation.

06:30.432 --> 06:32.851
I hope you won't end up back in the ER.

06:32.935 --> 06:34.394
It's not for me.

06:34.478 --> 06:35.854
It's for my little brother.

06:36.605 --> 06:37.564
You're a great sister.

06:39.108 --> 06:41.068
What, getting blackmailed
into doing his bidding?

06:41.735 --> 06:43.153
What does he have on you?

06:44.279 --> 06:48.033
Only two people found out about my secret.

06:50.077 --> 06:53.831
As usual, I was engrossed
in writing my novel…

06:55.874 --> 06:57.292
and talking to others online.

07:01.630 --> 07:05.175
Hey, I've got a random question.
What do you have our group chat saved as?

07:05.259 --> 07:07.094
Beautiful Life. BL.

07:07.177 --> 07:08.470
Real Estate Chat for me.

07:08.554 --> 07:10.764
Because sometimes,
my hubby looks at my phone.

07:12.266 --> 07:15.060
This is a rough draft
of something I'm working on.

07:15.144 --> 07:17.396
The characters
are a young master and his servant.

07:17.479 --> 07:18.730
Let me know what you think.

07:21.108 --> 07:22.609
That's such a great character dynamic.

07:23.610 --> 07:25.946
I don't get why your stuff
isn't more popular, Imuk.

07:26.029 --> 07:27.531
It's such a shame.

07:28.866 --> 07:32.161
Just imagine the beautiful young master
being heartbroken over the aloof servant.

07:33.120 --> 07:34.746
That just shot chills down my spine.

07:44.047 --> 07:44.965
I think

07:45.924 --> 07:49.720
there's someone behind me.

07:50.596 --> 07:51.722
Can it be a ghost?

07:52.431 --> 07:54.224
It'd be better if it were.

07:54.308 --> 07:56.018
If it's your parents, I'll pray for you.

08:23.045 --> 08:24.087
Did you see anything?

08:27.341 --> 08:30.761
Still, at least it wasn't my parents.

08:30.844 --> 08:33.722
But I do have to keep buying him coke
whenever he wants it.

08:35.057 --> 08:36.266
Why do you like it so much?

08:37.517 --> 08:39.019
I'm not sure.

08:39.102 --> 08:40.771
People like what they like.

08:42.689 --> 08:44.900
I guess that's why you kept writing
despite bombing every time.

08:45.943 --> 08:48.654
I always thought I'd hit it big
if I just kept on writing.

08:51.949 --> 08:53.492
That's unfounded confidence.

08:53.575 --> 08:56.870
If there were a basis for it,
that'd be a prophecy, not confidence.

08:57.913 --> 09:00.457
I'll keep at it,

09:00.540 --> 09:01.875
and I will get better.

09:05.754 --> 09:06.964
Sir.

09:07.047 --> 09:08.423
You know,

09:09.216 --> 09:11.301
back when EBC's crew came by to shoot,

09:11.927 --> 09:14.304
you didn't finish your answer
to my questions.

09:16.265 --> 09:19.351
I'm curious why you decided
to become a teacher.

09:37.035 --> 09:38.370
How was hanging out with your friend?

09:39.162 --> 09:40.038
Good.

09:44.251 --> 09:45.877
She's back for the first time in years

09:45.961 --> 09:47.754
and being feted
for winning the Fields Medal.

09:47.838 --> 09:50.757
And yet, she took the time
to come to Jeonju to see you.

09:50.841 --> 09:52.134
Why would she do that?

09:52.217 --> 09:54.469
This wasn't exactly a reunion
with your old Olympiad team.

09:54.553 --> 09:55.595
She came to see just you.

09:55.679 --> 09:56.888
No one else but you.

09:56.972 --> 09:58.265
Why is that?

09:59.099 --> 10:02.728
Did you share a warm and precious memory
from when you were both young?

10:02.811 --> 10:04.062
Did they use to date?

10:05.022 --> 10:07.190
That's the only explanation.

10:07.274 --> 10:10.402
When it comes to men and women,
it's all about the chemistry.

10:10.485 --> 10:13.071
There needs to be that spark

10:13.155 --> 10:16.616
for you to want to see that person again
after years have passed.

10:16.700 --> 10:18.201
-You know what I'm saying?
-True that.

10:18.285 --> 10:19.119
Mind your own business.

10:21.621 --> 10:22.706
Looks like you're right.

10:23.665 --> 10:24.499
Dude!

10:24.583 --> 10:26.043
I thought all you ever did was study.

10:27.627 --> 10:28.712
My guess is that

10:28.795 --> 10:32.049
Woo-su and this girl Deul-i

10:32.132 --> 10:34.801
hit it off at the Olympiad,
started dating, and then broke up.

10:34.885 --> 10:36.678
-No way.
-Hear me out.

10:36.762 --> 10:39.097
That must be why he dropped out.

10:39.181 --> 10:43.143
The thought of seeing his ex-girlfriend
pained his heart too much.

10:43.226 --> 10:44.936
-Been there.
-Just the thought

10:45.020 --> 10:46.438
upset him so much

10:46.521 --> 10:48.315
that he couldn't face it.

10:49.066 --> 10:53.236
Even our cold-hearted Woo-su
once felt the flicker of true love.

10:53.320 --> 10:54.196
Or something like that.

10:55.447 --> 10:56.573
I'm so proud of him.

10:56.656 --> 10:57.866
Still, he wouldn't just quit.

10:58.575 --> 10:59.618
Of course, he would.

11:00.494 --> 11:02.329
Why? Because they were rivals.

11:03.038 --> 11:04.122
Woo-su would have said,

11:07.042 --> 11:08.251
"I'll pull out

11:08.960 --> 11:10.754
so you can reach for the stars."
Or some such.

11:11.380 --> 11:12.506
Only one of them could win.

11:12.589 --> 11:16.551
You're saying Woo-su
gave up on math for a girl?

11:18.178 --> 11:20.931
Well, there was another reason as well.

11:22.140 --> 11:23.225
What?

11:25.811 --> 11:26.728
That thing.

11:27.562 --> 11:28.563
His phobia of being filmed.

11:29.981 --> 11:31.066
He feared finishing first.

11:37.406 --> 11:39.408
"Wow, that's amazing."

11:39.491 --> 11:41.159
"I can't believe
you have a student of your own."

11:42.953 --> 11:45.288
What's so amazing about that?

11:45.372 --> 11:47.416
Is it really so amazing
for a teacher to have students?

11:48.708 --> 11:50.460
Until next time, Eui-ju.

11:51.962 --> 11:52.879
"Next time"?

11:55.298 --> 11:56.133
Sure.

11:57.592 --> 11:59.302
Maybe we will meet again.

12:14.025 --> 12:17.362
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 7

12:32.377 --> 12:33.253
Who are you?

12:38.550 --> 12:39.551
Me?

12:40.218 --> 12:41.761
I'm the Chairwoman's secretary, Na Ran-i.

12:42.762 --> 12:46.433
As long as she pays me,
I take care of all her dirty work.

12:47.767 --> 12:49.811
She wants me to get you away from Si-on.

12:51.021 --> 12:52.898
As much as I appreciate your pretty face…

12:54.274 --> 12:55.567
This is it for you.

12:56.151 --> 12:57.277
No. Don't do it!

13:05.911 --> 13:07.746
Yoon!

13:08.747 --> 13:09.831
How did you find me?

13:41.696 --> 13:42.531
Yoon!

13:50.121 --> 13:50.997
Are you okay?

13:54.584 --> 13:55.835
I'm fine.

13:58.964 --> 14:01.174
SI-ON LOWERED HIMSELF TO MEET YOON'S EYES

14:01.758 --> 14:02.842
Let's get out of here.

14:05.554 --> 14:09.015
SO CLOSE AND SO INTENSE,
HIS GAZE MADE YOON'S HEART RACE

14:14.479 --> 14:16.231
JUST THEN, RAN-I CALLED OUT

14:16.314 --> 14:17.399
How amusing.

14:18.900 --> 14:21.111
Let's see how long you can keep this up.

14:21.736 --> 14:23.905
RAN-I'S COMMENT
PROVOKED YOON'S WILDER NATURE

14:23.989 --> 14:24.990
Just a moment.

14:26.074 --> 14:27.742
I refuse to be in anyone's debt.

14:28.868 --> 14:30.161
No!

14:30.245 --> 14:32.163
-Don't!
-Let it…

14:33.832 --> 14:35.458
YOON BID HER FAREWELL

14:35.542 --> 14:39.838
IT WAS FOR SI-ON, OF ALL PEOPLE

14:47.053 --> 14:50.223
CHAPTER 33:
SOMETHING UTTERLY USELESS

14:51.057 --> 14:52.767
-Eun Ha-su.
-Here.

14:53.435 --> 14:54.769
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

14:55.395 --> 14:56.771
-Choi Yu-mi.
-Here.

14:57.689 --> 14:59.441
-Yeo Eui-ju.
-Here.

15:00.025 --> 15:01.818
-Choi Go-ya.
-Here.

15:01.901 --> 15:02.736
Choi Ji-a.

15:07.449 --> 15:08.617
-Hong Su-min.
-Here.

15:08.700 --> 15:10.660
-Jeon Chae-won.
-Here.

15:10.744 --> 15:12.537
-Im Su-yeon.
-Here.

15:22.005 --> 15:23.423
-Im Su-yeon.
-Here.

15:23.506 --> 15:25.175
-Lee Eun-ji.
-Here.

15:25.258 --> 15:26.509
-Choi Hye-jeong.
-Here.

15:28.345 --> 15:29.596
I hope you're all ready for class.

15:31.723 --> 15:33.350
-I smell alcohol.
-What on earth?

15:33.433 --> 15:34.768
-It's definitely alcohol.
-What's this?

15:43.443 --> 15:44.944
Quiet.

15:48.365 --> 15:49.407
Who's on cleaning duty today?

15:50.283 --> 15:51.451
Me, sir.

15:52.827 --> 15:54.120
-Eui-ju.
-Yes, sir?

15:54.746 --> 15:56.748
-Clean up again.
-Yes, sir.

15:56.831 --> 15:58.958
-Let's air out the room. Open the windows.
-But it's cold.

16:03.213 --> 16:04.381
Ji-a, go to the nurse's office.

16:24.025 --> 16:25.193
Morning to you too.

16:31.574 --> 16:32.450
Hey!

16:43.628 --> 16:44.963
Mr. Ga.

16:45.046 --> 16:47.006
She's in your class, right?

16:47.090 --> 16:49.634
Are you aware she's come to school drunk?

16:50.218 --> 16:52.679
Goodness me.

16:52.762 --> 16:56.433
How can a student come to school
reeking of alcohol?

17:01.604 --> 17:05.358
You're the one who wasn't in her uniform
when the EBC crew was here filming.

17:05.442 --> 17:08.570
Are you taking school seriously?

17:08.653 --> 17:13.032
Ms. Kim, let me get back to you
after hearing Ji-a's side of the story.

17:14.492 --> 17:15.910
Mr. Ga.

17:15.994 --> 17:18.496
This student is drunk.

17:18.580 --> 17:20.749
What is there to understand?

17:23.960 --> 17:25.128
Step out for a moment.

17:33.094 --> 17:35.388
I don't want to butt heads
with you over nothing.

17:36.848 --> 17:39.851
I finally got rid of that knot yesterday,
and I'm starting to tense up again.

17:41.603 --> 17:45.356
Ji-a's background differs somewhat
from that of other students.

17:45.440 --> 17:46.900
She has no parental support.

17:46.983 --> 17:49.569
She's staying at a youth shelter
and must earn a living herself.

17:49.652 --> 17:53.281
Despite that,
she still has a strong desire to learn.

17:53.364 --> 17:55.241
Really?

17:55.325 --> 17:56.659
That's great.

17:56.743 --> 17:59.078
Then, she'll surely do well
at another school.

17:59.662 --> 18:01.498
She might seem tough,
but she's still just a child.

18:04.250 --> 18:06.920
As her homeroom teacher,
I'd like to personally make sure

18:07.504 --> 18:09.589
she turns her life around.

18:10.673 --> 18:12.091
Please allow me that opportunity.

18:12.175 --> 18:13.468
Mr. Ga.

18:13.551 --> 18:15.470
Do you recall our school motto?

18:16.221 --> 18:19.140
It's "Aim for the Elite."

18:19.933 --> 18:22.101
I can't seem to imagine her career choices

18:22.185 --> 18:25.313
or her life goals of any kind

18:26.022 --> 18:27.857
being anywhere near that ideal.

18:28.358 --> 18:31.110
In other words,
she's not a good fit for this school.

18:32.612 --> 18:34.155
You may leave.

18:44.249 --> 18:47.001
Does he think he's a crusader for justice?

18:47.085 --> 18:50.421
Of all the students to stick up for,
he chose the one who showed up drunk.

18:51.047 --> 18:52.257
How obnoxious.

18:53.424 --> 18:56.135
Would you believe
he's friends with Na Deul-i?

18:56.219 --> 18:57.720
Who is Na Deul-i?

18:57.804 --> 18:59.889
Don't you know, Aunt Young-hee?

18:59.973 --> 19:02.642
She's the Fields Medal winner.
Apparently, they're friends.

19:03.810 --> 19:04.978
What?

19:05.520 --> 19:07.981
You're unbelievable.

19:08.064 --> 19:10.066
Why are you only mentioning this now?

19:10.149 --> 19:11.776
When else did I have the chance?

19:17.907 --> 19:18.783
Ji-a.

19:22.829 --> 19:23.663
Why did you do it?

19:26.082 --> 19:28.334
It's wrong for a student
to come to school drunk.

19:31.337 --> 19:33.840
Anyone can make a mistake.
It's what's next that's important.

19:33.923 --> 19:38.177
Write an essay stating what you did wrong
and what you're going to do about it.

19:38.803 --> 19:40.680
I will show it to the principal.

19:42.140 --> 19:43.057
Yes, sir.

19:44.017 --> 19:46.352
I'll get you a lighter punishment,
so be sure to wear your uniform

19:46.436 --> 19:47.478
and don't skip class

19:48.313 --> 19:49.272
or get into any trouble.

19:50.315 --> 19:51.232
Yes, sir.

19:57.322 --> 19:58.990
-That's for sure.
-I can't take it.

19:59.073 --> 19:59.908
Eui-ju, over here!

19:59.991 --> 20:01.743
Eui-ju, quickly!

20:02.785 --> 20:05.079
-I don't know.
-This is so good.

20:05.163 --> 20:06.497
-Try it. It's incredible.
-Let's see.

20:06.581 --> 20:07.790
Where are you off to, Go-ya?

20:09.500 --> 20:10.710
Can I sit here?

20:12.295 --> 20:13.630
Sit down, Eui-ju.

20:13.713 --> 20:14.714
Okay.

20:17.425 --> 20:19.636
The food is so good today!

20:20.637 --> 20:22.263
Eat up. It's delish.

20:26.184 --> 20:27.560
Can I have a minute, Go-ya?

20:31.773 --> 20:33.399
Go-ya, where are you going?

20:34.776 --> 20:36.819
-I have huge news.
-What is it?

20:36.903 --> 20:39.072
Young-hee wanted to expel Ji-a,

20:39.155 --> 20:41.074
but Mr. Ga stopped her.

20:41.157 --> 20:42.659
-Really?
-That's amazing.

20:42.742 --> 20:43.910
Seems like it's on hold.

20:44.786 --> 20:48.164
Gosh. How did he manage that?

20:48.247 --> 20:49.832
He must have some kind of leverage.

20:51.834 --> 20:54.337
When are you going to make up with Go-ya?

20:54.420 --> 20:57.131
I have to say everything twice.

20:57.215 --> 20:58.383
It sucks.

20:58.466 --> 21:02.762
Is Go-ya still refusing to talk to you?

21:03.721 --> 21:04.555
Yeah.

21:05.348 --> 21:08.810
What did you guys argue about, anyway?

21:11.604 --> 21:12.855
Argue?

21:13.481 --> 21:14.649
We didn't argue.

21:14.732 --> 21:17.193
-What is it?
-Oh, please.

21:17.276 --> 21:18.653
Just tell us.

21:27.787 --> 21:29.747
I have a research idea
I'd like to work on with you.

21:33.001 --> 21:35.628
You were always
the most interesting person to talk to.

21:37.964 --> 21:39.757
I don't know how long it will take,

21:39.841 --> 21:41.801
but I really want to work with you

21:42.385 --> 21:44.303
on the topology
of algebraic curves and surfaces.

21:48.683 --> 21:49.851
Why that topic?

21:51.310 --> 21:53.604
I'm not sure. It just drew me in.

21:54.313 --> 21:55.898
I was looking
for something utterly useless.

21:59.819 --> 22:01.070
Remember that Hardy quote?

22:01.154 --> 22:04.157
"No discovery of mine has made,
or is likely to make,

22:04.240 --> 22:06.451
directly or indirectly,

22:06.534 --> 22:08.202
for good or ill,

22:08.286 --> 22:10.413
the least difference

22:10.496 --> 22:12.165
to the amenity of the world."

22:12.665 --> 22:13.499
"I have

22:13.583 --> 22:17.086
-never done anything useful."
-"…never done anything useful."

22:22.341 --> 22:23.843
That's my next goal.

22:24.510 --> 22:26.387
Accomplishing something utterly useless.

22:43.696 --> 22:44.822
Where are you going?

22:44.906 --> 22:45.740
For a walk.

22:46.365 --> 22:48.785
I'll go with you.
I need to walk off my dinner.

22:51.287 --> 22:52.830
Are you still getting bad headaches?

22:52.914 --> 22:53.748
Sometimes.

22:54.499 --> 22:55.958
Shouldn't you see a doctor?

22:56.042 --> 22:57.210
It's not that bad.

22:57.835 --> 22:59.462
Just go anyway.

22:59.545 --> 23:01.297
There's no harm in getting checked out.

23:01.380 --> 23:02.548
Fine. I'll go.

23:03.341 --> 23:05.009
No empty promises, all right?

23:05.093 --> 23:06.135
Make sure you go.

23:07.178 --> 23:08.054
Okay.

23:19.982 --> 23:21.275
Get me a coke on your way home.

23:23.694 --> 23:26.864
I'm already home.

23:30.034 --> 23:31.494
I'm in my room.

23:31.577 --> 23:33.162
Can I get it tomorrow instead?

23:35.039 --> 23:36.040
Mom!

23:36.124 --> 23:37.708
I have something to tell you.

23:37.792 --> 23:39.210
Hey, Eui-do!

23:39.293 --> 23:41.170
Okay, Eui-do. I get it, all right?

23:41.254 --> 23:42.171
I'll go now.

24:02.775 --> 24:04.735
About that proposal
from your friend Deul-i.

24:05.403 --> 24:06.404
What do you think?

24:07.029 --> 24:07.905
Be honest.

24:08.698 --> 24:10.449
I don't know. I'm not interested.

24:11.284 --> 24:12.160
Liar.

24:13.161 --> 24:14.871
You answered too quickly

24:14.954 --> 24:16.038
like you'd rehearsed it.

24:17.707 --> 24:21.544
I wish you'd do what you really want to.

24:22.712 --> 24:25.006
So seize this opportunity
and go to the US.

24:25.089 --> 24:26.382
Go do the research you want to do

24:27.258 --> 24:28.176
before it's too late.

24:29.719 --> 24:31.137
Are you going to the US?

25:08.758 --> 25:10.301
It's late. Go home.

25:10.384 --> 25:11.219
I don't want to.

25:11.302 --> 25:13.179
To tell the truth, I…

25:13.262 --> 25:14.931
I told you
I never wanted to see you again.

25:15.014 --> 25:16.265
What am I going to do now?

25:16.974 --> 25:18.059
How come you're here?

25:18.142 --> 25:19.310
Sir! What do we do?

25:19.393 --> 25:21.229
Why isn't she answering?

25:21.312 --> 25:22.438
Why isn't she even checking?

25:22.521 --> 25:24.732
-Hurry up and leave.
-Sir!

25:24.815 --> 25:26.609
I see you still haven't figured me out.

25:26.692 --> 25:28.903
"You're going down for real then."

25:28.986 --> 25:30.154
So cool.

25:30.238 --> 25:32.907
He's so cool.

25:32.990 --> 25:33.950
Tell him how you feel.

25:34.033 --> 25:36.327
To show him how serious you are,
look him in the eye.

25:36.410 --> 25:37.787
-I…
-For at least three seconds.

25:38.621 --> 25:40.164
Look him in the eye for three seconds.

26:36.595 --> 26:38.597
Subtitle: Paul Carver
